---
title: Pasta with Saffron, Corn, and Harissa Breadcrumbs
source: direct-input
servings: 4
description: Recipe credit [@lahbco](https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db8ZrcIOIiK/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==)
---

Prep the @corn{4}(kernels removed) by removing the kernels from the cobs, and composting the cobs (or save for stock). Set aside. In a bowl, add 1 ice cube and add @saffron threads{12} to it. Let the ice completely melt until it turns a beautiful orange hue. Set aside. In a #skillet{}, heat @butter{3%tbsp} over medium-low heat. Add the @onion{1}(minced) and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and sauté until softened, about ~{6%minutes}.

Add the corn kernels and saffron water then sauté for about ~{4%minutes} until the corn is a bright yellow. Season with a pinch of @kosher salt{}.

Cook your @pasta{} in heavily salted water until al dente. Reserve @pasta water{3/4 cup} and drain and add back to the pot. Using an immersion blender, combine the sautéed corn, @pasta water{1/2 cup}, @almond milk{1/4 cup}, and @white miso{1%tbsp} until smooth. Taste and add @salt{} if needed. Toss with the cooked pasta and the remaining @pasta water{} over medium heat until emulsified.

To make the breadcrumbs: Melt @butter{2%tbsp} over medium heat in a pan. Add @panko breadcrumbs{3/4 cup} and toast until golden brown. Sprinkle @harissa seasoning{1%tsp} over the panko and toss to coat. Remove from heat and toss with @parsley{2%tbsp}(chopped).

Serve pasta with a sprinkle of harissa breadcrumbs on top and cracked @black pepper{}.